        "original_id": "17a95c5b-b1fa-55b0-bbe0-51dc1cf73d0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Ixia, Rhexia, Ixia polystachya\n- Places: South Africa, Cape\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Ixia is a genus of cormous plants native to South Africa.\n- Ixia belongs to the family Iridaceae and the subfamily Ixioideae.\n- Rhexia is a plant genus in the family Melastomataceae.\n- Melastomataceae has about 4,500 species in 150 genera.\n- Ixia polystachya is a species in the genus Ixia.\n- Ixia polystachya is also called white-and-yellow-flower cornlily.\n- Ixia polystachya is found on hills and slopes in the northwest and southwest Cape of South Africa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
